 "notes": {
  "legend": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 1000,
   "page": "launch",
   "size": 24,
   "text": "How to read this canvas\n\n• Components are the real HalalGoes design-system components. A dashed grey tag \"Proposed component: <name>\" marks a composite built only from library parts and design-system components, for the owner to approve into the design system.\n• A dashed blue tag \"Needs API: <what>\" marks data or actions the contract does not provide. Nothing marked so is designed as real.\n• Every amount is server integer cents through Price. Nothing is added up in the browser. No tax line.\n• Colours are role tokens from the design system's own tokens.css; the canvas has no local token overrides.\n• Desktop working pages fit 1440 × 900 and never scroll as a page. Long lists scroll inside their own region. Details open in a panel beside the page, never over it.\n• The restaurant web ships light only, and at launch every restaurant login is its owner.\n• Artboards that need later-version operations are on the page \"Later version (not in launch)\".",
   "w": 520,
   "x": -620,
   "y": -1300
  },
  "n-later": {
   "fill": "orange",
   "maxH": 1000,
   "page": "later",
   "size": 24,
   "text": "Not in launch\n\nThese artboards use later-version operations: listNotifications (the bell) and restaurant two-step sign-in (enrollTotp).\n\nPayout history and each payout's detail moved to the Launch page: the owner moved listRestaurantPayouts into launch (round 2 decision).",
   "w": 520,
   "x": -620,
   "y": 0
  },
  "n-payouts": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 900,
   "page": "launch",
   "size": 24,
   "text": "Payouts at launch\n\nThe payout account (getConnectStatus: payouts on or on hold, bank ending, how often, what Stripe needs) and, since the owner moved listRestaurantPayouts into launch, the payout history and each payout's detail (rows further down this page). See your payouts on the account page opens the history. The bell stays a later version, so history pages show none.\n\nWhen Stripe restricts payouts on an account that worked before, the restaurant keeps taking orders; earnings are kept on record and paid out once Stripe has what it needs (owner decision). A restaurant that never finished Stripe setup cannot go live (owner decision): the setup banners say so only for live accounts. Needs API: tell 'never set up' apart from 'restricted later'.",
   "w": 520,
   "x": -620,
   "y": 1340
  },
  "n-strip": {
   "fill": "orange",
   "maxH": 1100,
   "page": "launch",
   "size": 24,
   "text": "Orders waiting: the strip\n\nThe header, under the app bar (owner decision). It sits where the eye already is, it never competes with a panel's Save or Send at the bottom, and on the kitchen tablet it isn't hidden by the browser's own bottom bar.\n\nEvery order awaiting acceptance is listed, soonest to expire first, each with its 3-minute countdown from the server. The focused order shows Accept (the one primary action, 72 px) and Reject; the rest stay compact.\n\nKeys: ← → move, A accepts, R opens the reason panel. They act only while focus is inside the strip, so a stray keypress can't accept an order.\n\nEvery page that shows the orders strip sends sendRestaurantHeartbeat every 30 s. Closed-offline therefore means this browser lost its connection, not that the Orders page is closed.\n\nAccept captures the payment. If it goes through, the order leaves the strip with a confirmation that links to it. If the capture fails for good, the order is cancelled and the strip says not to prepare it. If time runs out while the reason panel is open, the panel says it was turned down automatically.\n\nThe alert sound keeps ringing until each order is accepted, rejected or expires. The customer's phone stays hidden until the order is accepted.",
   "w": 520,
   "x": -620,
   "y": 0
  },
  "n-support": {
   "fill": "blue",
   "maxH": 900,
   "page": "launch",
   "size": 24,
   "text": "Contact support\n\nNo support endpoint exists. Phone and hours come from getPublicConfig; the email address is a sample until PublicConfig carries it. Certificates and ID are never sent by email.",
   "w": 520,
   "x": -620,
   "y": 9980
  },
